{"real": true, "dur": 84.7, "sent": [{"start": 0.18, "end": 5.7, "text": "There’s another idea I can use in both languages, and I think it could work in others too.", "words": [{"w": "There’s", "s": 0.18}, {"w": "another", "s": 0.52}, {"w": "idea", "s": 0.96}, {"w": "I", "s": 1.38}, {"w": "can", "s": 1.48}, {"w": "use", "s": 1.72}, {"w": "in", "s": 1.94}, {"w": "both", "s": 2.14}, {"w": "languages,", "s": 2.44}, {"w": "and", "s": 3.7}, {"w": "I", "s": 3.94}, {"w": "think", "s": 4.08}, {"w": "it", "s": 4.32}, {"w": "could", "s": 4.42}, {"w": "work", "s": 4.66}, {"w": "in", "s": 4.88}, {"w": "others", "s": 5.08}, {"w": "too.", "s": 5.46}]}, {"start": 6.64, "end": 8.48, "text": "I call it the transfer test.", "words": [{"w": "I", "s": 6.64}, {"w": "call", "s": 6.78}, {"w": "it", "s": 7.02}, {"w": "the", "s": 7.44}, {"w": "transfer", "s": 7.6}, {"w": "test.", "s": 8.119}]}, {"start": 9.22, "end": 10.12, "text": "Here’s how it works.", "words": [{"w": "Here’s", "s": 9.22}, {"w": "how", "s": 9.46}, {"w": "it", "s": 9.64}, {"w": "works.", "s": 9.78}]}, {"start": 10.54, "end": 16.78, "text": "At the end of an exercise run, I ask learners about a word they’ve never seen before.", "words": [{"w": "At", "s": 10.54}, {"w": "the", "s": 10.72}, {"w": "end", "s": 10.94}, {"w": "of", "s": 11.14}, {"w": "an", "s": 11.28}, {"w": "exercise", "s": 11.48}, {"w": "run,", "s": 12.16}, {"w": "I", "s": 13.3}, {"w": "ask", "s": 13.52}, {"w": "learners", "s": 13.8}, {"w": "about", "s": 14.54}, {"w": "a", "s": 14.88}, {"w": "word", "s": 15.04}, {"w": "they’ve", "s": 15.48}, {"w": "never", "s": 15.8}, {"w": "seen", "s": 16.1}, {"w": "before.", "s": 16.36}]}, {"start": 17.2, "end": 29.52, "text": "In French, for example, the course teaches the masculine and feminine words for “a Chinese person.” Then it asks: what about Luxembourgish?", "words": [{"w": "In", "s": 17.2}, {"w": "French,", "s": 17.42}, {"w": "for", "s": 18.42}, {"w": "example,", "s": 18.58}, {"w": "the", "s": 19.72}, {"w": "course", "s": 19.9}, {"w": "teaches", "s": 20.6}, {"w": "the", "s": 21.38}, {"w": "masculine", "s": 21.54}, {"w": "and", "s": 22.54}, {"w": "feminine", "s": 22.78}, {"w": "words", "s": 23.28}, {"w": "for", "s": 24.02}, {"w": "“a", "s": 24.26}, {"w": "Chinese", "s": 24.7}, {"w": "person.”", "s": 25.2}, {"w": "Then", "s": 26.62}, {"w": "it", "s": 27.12}, {"w": "asks:", "s": 27.38}, {"w": "what", "s": 28.24}, {"w": "about", "s": 28.46}, {"w": "Luxembourgish?", "s": 28.74}]}, {"start": 30.18, "end": 31.34, "text": "Nobody taught that one.", "words": [{"w": "Nobody", "s": 30.18}, {"w": "taught", "s": 30.66}, {"w": "that", "s": 30.92}, {"w": "one.", "s": 31.14}]}, {"start": 31.78, "end": 36.36, "text": "But learners know the rule: if the word ends in -s, you add -e.", "words": [{"w": "But", "s": 31.78}, {"w": "learners", "s": 32.0}, {"w": "know", "s": 32.38}, {"w": "the", "s": 32.619}, {"w": "rule:", "s": 32.78}, {"w": "if", "s": 33.52}, {"w": "the", "s": 33.7}, {"w": "word", "s": 33.86}, {"w": "ends", "s": 34.28}, {"w": "in", "s": 34.62}, {"w": "-s,", "s": 34.72}, {"w": "you", "s": 35.62}, {"w": "add", "s": 35.8}, {"w": "-e.", "s": 35.98}]}, {"start": 37.18, "end": 40.1, "text": "So they can work out the answer by applying the rule.", "words": [{"w": "So", "s": 37.18}, {"w": "they", "s": 37.4}, {"w": "can", "s": 37.56}, {"w": "work", "s": 37.78}, {"w": "out", "s": 38.02}, {"w": "the", "s": 38.18}, {"w": "answer", "s": 38.4}, {"w": "by", "s": 39.06}, {"w": "applying", "s": 39.28}, {"w": "the", "s": 39.76}, {"w": "rule.", "s": 39.9}]}, {"start": 40.86, "end": 42.3, "text": "You can see it happening here.", "words": [{"w": "You", "s": 40.86}, {"w": "can", "s": 40.98}, {"w": "see", "s": 41.24}, {"w": "it", "s": 41.42}, {"w": "happening", "s": 41.58}, {"w": "here.", "s": 42.06}]}, {"start": 43.14, "end": 45.5, "text": "However, that answer isn’t marked.", "words": [{"w": "However,", "s": 43.14}, {"w": "that", "s": 44.0}, {"w": "answer", "s": 44.3}, {"w": "isn’t", "s": 44.86}, {"w": "marked.", "s": 45.2}]}, {"start": 45.82, "end": 50.1, "text": "After all, you can’t mark someone wrong on something you never told them.", "words": [{"w": "After", "s": 45.82}, {"w": "all,", "s": 46.18}, {"w": "you", "s": 47.02}, {"w": "can’t", "s": 47.18}, {"w": "mark", "s": 47.44}, {"w": "someone", "s": 47.72}, {"w": "wrong", "s": 48.08}, {"w": "on", "s": 48.52}, {"w": "something", "s": 48.72}, {"w": "you", "s": 49.14}, {"w": "never", "s": 49.32}, {"w": "told", "s": 49.64}, {"w": "them.", "s": 49.9}]}, {"start": 50.86, "end": 54.14, "text": "Instead, the feedback simply gives them the rule.", "words": [{"w": "Instead,", "s": 50.86}, {"w": "the", "s": 51.66}, {"w": "feedback", "s": 51.82}, {"w": "simply", "s": 52.38}, {"w": "gives", "s": 52.92}, {"w": "them", "s": 53.24}, {"w": "the", "s": 53.76}, {"w": "rule.", "s": 53.9}]}, {"start": 54.48, "end": 63.28, "text": "Chinese works the same way, and the rule’s even simpler: country plus the word for “person” gives you the nationality.", "words": [{"w": "Chinese", "s": 54.48}, {"w": "works", "s": 54.94}, {"w": "the", "s": 55.38}, {"w": "same", "s": 55.6}, {"w": "way,", "s": 55.9}, {"w": "and", "s": 56.92}, {"w": "the", "s": 57.08}, {"w": "rule’s", "s": 57.26}, {"w": "even", "s": 57.76}, {"w": "simpler:", "s": 58.14}, {"w": "country", "s": 59.3}, {"w": "plus", "s": 59.88}, {"w": "the", "s": 60.14}, {"w": "word", "s": 60.28}, {"w": "for", "s": 60.52}, {"w": "“person”", "s": 60.62}, {"w": "gives", "s": 61.88}, {"w": "you", "s": 62.14}, {"w": "the", "s": 62.38}, {"w": "nationality.", "s": 62.52}]}, {"start": 63.68, "end": 72.34, "text": "For example, China gives you “a Chinese person.” And Britain gives you “a British person.” Then: Luxembourg?", "words": [{"w": "For", "s": 63.68}, {"w": "example,", "s": 63.9}, {"w": "China", "s": 64.98}, {"w": "gives", "s": 65.34}, {"w": "you", "s": 65.64}, {"w": "“a", "s": 65.76}, {"w": "Chinese", "s": 66.3}, {"w": "person.”", "s": 66.76}, {"w": "And", "s": 68.04}, {"w": "Britain", "s": 68.24}, {"w": "gives", "s": 68.62}, {"w": "you", "s": 68.88}, {"w": "“a", "s": 69.0}, {"w": "British", "s": 69.58}, {"w": "person.”", "s": 70.04}, {"w": "Then:", "s": 71.32}, {"w": "Luxembourg?", "s": 71.82}]}, {"start": 73.24, "end": 75.48, "text": "Same pattern, and here’s the answer.", "words": [{"w": "Same", "s": 73.24}, {"w": "pattern,", "s": 73.5}, {"w": "and", "s": 74.46}, {"w": "here’s", "s": 74.66}, {"w": "the", "s": 74.96}, {"w": "answer.", "s": 75.1}]}, {"start": 75.94, "end": 84.12, "text": "In the end, that helps me see whether learners have understood the rule or simply memorised the examples.", "words": [{"w": "In", "s": 75.94}, {"w": "the", "s": 76.06}, {"w": "end,", "s": 76.22}, {"w": "that", "s": 77.36}, {"w": "helps", "s": 77.64}, {"w": "me", "s": 77.94}, {"w": "see", "s": 78.28}, {"w": "whether", "s": 78.9}, {"w": "learners", "s": 79.26}, {"w": "have", "s": 80.0}, {"w": "understood", "s": 80.28}, {"w": "the", "s": 80.82}, {"w": "rule", "s": 80.98}, {"w": "or", "s": 81.68}, {"w": "simply", "s": 81.88}, {"w": "memorised", "s": 82.62}, {"w": "the", "s": 83.3}, {"w": "examples.", "s": 83.46}]}]}